  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSSP - Civil Society Support Programme 2013-2016 - Civil Society Support Programme - CSSP</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CSSP - Civil Society Support Programme 2013-2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CSSP is a joint Donor Pooled Funding of Civil Society Organisations.  Currently, It is aimed at building the capacity of Civil Societies to respond to local needs. Currently, it is funded by Irish Aid, DfID    and the Netherlands. Sweden is joining the programme in 2012.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSSP is a joint Donor Pooled Funding of Civil Society Organisations.  Currently, it is funded by Irish Aid, DfID and the Netherlands. It is aimed at building the capacity of Civil Societies to respond to local needs. Currently, it is funded by Irish Aid, DfID and the             Netherlands. Sweden is joining the programme in 2012.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the CSSP&#xa0;are as follows:
1. Critical mass of civil society organisations which have the capability to: i) respond to development priorities determined by poor women, men, girls and boys - especially those in &apos;hard to reach&apos; categories, and ii) operate as robust, accountable and legitimate organisations.
2. More civil society organisations which have the capacity to dialogue, and relate with, a range of different constituencies and stakeholders.
3. Mutual accountability for efficient and effective performance of the different actors which comprise the CSSP delivery mechanism: the Development Partners individually and as part of the CSSP Management Board (CMB) and Programme Steering Committee (PSC) including its sub-groups, the Lead Development Partner (LDP) and the Management Agent (MA) and CSSP team.</narrative>
  </description>
